{"title":"Uncountable","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is said to be <b>uncountable</b> if there is no <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Injection\" title=\"Injection\">injection</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/7/0672981893451e9ef219c3613ffa6e19d5988b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:S\\to\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. Assuming the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Axiom_of_choice\" title=\"Axiom of choice\">Axiom of choice</a>, every set that is <i>not</i> uncountable is either <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Finite\" title=\"Finite\">finite</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Countably_infinite&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Countably infinite (page does not exist)\">countably infinite</a>.  The most common example of an uncountable set is the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_that_is_uncountable\">Proof that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is uncountable</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Uncountable&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof that  is uncountable\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We give an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indirect_proof&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Indirect proof (page does not exist)\">indirect proof</a> here. This is one of the most famous indirect proofs and was first given by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Georg_Cantor\" title=\"Georg Cantor\">Georg Cantor</a>.\n</p><p>Suppose that the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee856b92e7431c666a70bca1c6a78e1f7ff0f5b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}:0&lt;x&lt; 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" /> is countable. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f67c710b8f8a482e104bad13f5cd031202de00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\omega_1, \\omega_2, \\omega_3, ...\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> be any enumeration of the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> (in other words, take an injection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8468dda4e4a123c33fa546c0f013b3afbaf864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: A \\to \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />, and denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/2580289fc9b5cebe1eea28ca22fe76d6e531c11a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_i = f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p><p>Consider the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Decimal_expansion\" title=\"Decimal expansion\">decimal expansion</a> of each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fc80d5e036efbaf3de0e9dab053194a1e6676ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266b8366be193d9436c23f3de4afa7eac5e54547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_i=0.b_{i1}b_{i2}b_{i3} \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.  Now construct a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/3180ff4c9389c381c7ccfd6ff92ad7113bdc6e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega= 0.b_1b_2b_3 \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />, by choosing the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> so that it differs from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aaedfdd8093bc23698872e5fe561634e7db09a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{ii}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> by at least 3 and so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> is never equal to 9 or 0.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> differs from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fc80d5e036efbaf3de0e9dab053194a1e6676ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> by at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/9793db5d37321ca16a33379411779d9365fd61e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{10^i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28055a191f1d1cad99e14df56251894cdf3175f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega \\neq \\omega_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be7d73d99cbf0c9cd46238bf84423e48131a1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega \\not \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />.  However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is clearly a real number between 0 and 1, a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Contradiction\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Contradiction\">contradiction</a>.  Thus our assumption that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is countable must be false, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd10b290599f0f04a5a4a94b655a40116d44b10e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R} \\supset A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is uncountable.\n</p><p>An alternative proof uses <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cantor%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Cantor&#39;s Theorem (page does not exist)\">Cantor's Theorem</a>, which says that for all sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48ce9e1e60be1e8939bb474a843750318b7a4a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|&lt;|\\mathcal{P}(S)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51deaac5e024665f8d409987d79bf82bf618f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_set\" title=\"Power set\">power set</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. First, we note that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cantor_set\" title=\"Cantor set\">Cantor set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecbfb5e7dd547c1e0ca2eeb4669f2cc7f1ae4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> has cardinality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fccc1b10623f60d883fe207aba1671132227c194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{\\aleph_{0}}&gt;\\aleph_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64fe42473d0c079feb3d7d9c333aab15ff3cd321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}\\subset\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, there is an injection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/912acc1085e9fa3247443c1d7bc56a9318ad55a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathcal{C}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b58d6c75ccf6e21f210ab72627b832da748396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\mathbb{R}|\\geq 2^{\\aleph_{0}}&gt;\\aleph_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is uncountable. In fact, it turns out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa073b7c80c1713e1c0754c55f8ba48cc6aca8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\mathbb{R}|=2^{\\aleph_{0}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Uncountable&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Countable\" title=\"Countable\">Countable</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infinite\" title=\"Infinite\">Infinite</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Finite\" title=\"Finite\">Finite</a></li></ul>\n<p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Uncountable&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003730\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 208/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6883/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.485      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.485      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2243:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003730 and revision id 110292. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}